Goal: The code and data in this project is used to produce the reported results of testing a Delta-Sigma circuit model. 

Software Requirements: 
- Matlab/Simulink R2022a or more recent versions
- A supported C/C++ compiler to compile the MEX files that the tool BREACH needs. To check this, type 'mex -setup' 
and 'mex -setup C++' 


Contents:
- breach-dev: this directory contains the BREACH tool for falsification purposes.
- the directories "ExampleBand-Pass" and "Functions" contains the Simulink models and matlab code used to encode 
and simulate the Delta-Sigma model.
- three directories SigExpA, SigExpB, SigExpC contain the timed words generated from the expressions 
exA, exB, exC in the EMSOFT2026 paper. The timed words are stored in files with names having the prefix "s_". 
The files with names having with the prefix "f1cos_clean_s" are continuous-time signals 
(having peaks of varying width) generated from timed words. 
- matlab files: 
    - testUniform.m (the main file to produce the results), 
    - data_cleaning.m and continuous_signal_generation.m (to transform timed words to continuous-time signals with peaks of varying width), 
    -piecewise_cos.m (auxiliary function used by continuous_signal_generation.m



To produce the results report in the paper, 
1. Install Breach: go to the directory "breach-dev" and type "InstallBreach"
2. From the xecute the script 'testUniform.m'. To plot the falsifiers, 
set the variable 'display_option' in this script to a value greater than 0.

The execution will report: no falsifiers for signals from exC, and more falsifiers from exA  
than from exB. 



